        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Firefox 158 supports WebGPU clip-distances feature]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30844</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30844"/>
        <updated>2026-10-12T07:07:47.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Firefox 158 supports the WebGPU <code class="notranslate">clip-distances</code> feature, on macOS on Apple silicon only: <a href="https://bugzil.la/1931629" rel="nofollow">https://bugzil.la/1931629</a></li>
<li>Windows isn't supported, as the DX12 backend doesn't report the feature: <a href="https://bugzil.la/2073506" rel="nofollow">https://bugzil.la/2073506</a></li>
<li>Added the same partial notes as <a href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30783" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30783/hovercard"><code class="notranslate">feature_float32-blendable</code></a>, plus Windows, and set <code class="notranslate">firefox_android</code> to <code class="notranslate">false</code></li>
<li>Set <code class="notranslate">experimental</code> to <code class="notranslate">false</code>: now supported in Chromium and Gecko</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Firefox 159 Nightly on macOS: <code class="notranslate">adapter.features</code> lists <code class="notranslate">clip-distances</code>, <code class="notranslate">requestDevice({ requiredFeatures: ["clip-distances"] })</code> resolves, and a shader with <code class="notranslate">enable clip_distances;</code> and <code class="notranslate">@builtin(clip_distances)</code> creates a render pipeline without errors</li>
<li>Firefox 157 on macOS: <code class="notranslate">requestDevice()</code> rejects with "'clip-distances' was requested in <code class="notranslate">requiredFeatures</code>, but it is not supported by Firefox"</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5617206383" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45890" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/45890/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45890">mdn/content#45890</a></li>
</ul>]]></content>
